# 94. Conversational Reporting, Evidence and Explanation

When Artemis reports what happened, it must report from canonical evidence.

The conversational model must not invent an operational history.

## 94.1 Canonical Report Sources

Questions such as:

- `What did you do today?`
- `Why did you disable that source?`
- `Which Agent changed?`
- `How many trades did you make?`
- `What failed?`

must be answered from the relevant canonical sources such as:

- Action Ledger
- Decision Ledger
- Agent run history
- Trading/order history
- Configuration history
- Task state
- Audit records
- Provider/runtime health
- Reconciliation state

## 94.2 Lifecycle Truthfulness

Reports must distinguish:

- Proposed
- Planned
- Awaiting approval
- Approved
- Started
- Executed
- Verification pending
- Verified
- Failed
- Partially completed
- Rolled back
- Reconciled
- Cancelled

Do not say `done` merely because Artemis created a plan or tool call.

## 94.3 Explainability Commands

The ACCP should support natural-language requests equivalent to:

- WHY
- SHOW_EVIDENCE
- SHOW_CHANGE
- SHOW_STATUS
- SHOW_LIMITATIONS

Where available, Artemis should explain:

- What it concluded
- What evidence it used
- What it excluded
- Which policy blocked or allowed an action
- What changed
- What remains uncertain

## 94.4 Financial Reporting

Financial action reports must be based on reconciled or appropriately qualified
canonical trading/account data.

Do not report expected P&L as realized P&L.

Do not report order submission as order fill.

## 94.5 Redaction

Evidence shown through chat must preserve:

- Secret redaction
- User/tenant privacy
- Role authorization
- Sensitive-log filtering

`Show me everything` is not authorization to expose protected data.

